---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy policy" description="Prismbyte privacy policy." canonical={`${site.url}/privacy-policy/`}>
  <div class="container">
    <header class="page-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    </header>

    <article class="static-page">
      <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
      <p>
        This privacy policy explains how Prismbyte ("we", "us", "our") collects, uses, and shares information when you visit prismbyte.site ("the website"). It explains what information we collect, how we use it, and who we share it with.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Information we collect</h2>
      <h3>Newsletter email address</h3>
      <p>
        If you subscribe to our newsletter through the newsletter signup form, we collect your email address. This email address is submitted to Brevo, our email service provider, for subscription management.
      </p>
      <h3>Website usage data</h3>
      <p>
        When you visit our website, we automatically collect your page URL, page title, and page path through Google Tag Manager and Google Analytics 4.
      </p>
      <h3>Affiliate link clicks</h3>
      <p>
        When you click on an affiliate link on our website, we record the affiliate product name, link URL, link text, page URL, and page title. This data is used for attribution and editorial analysis.
      </p>

      <h2>3. How we collect information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Directly from you:</strong> When you submit your email address through the newsletter signup form on the homepage.</li>
        <li><strong>Automatically:</strong> Google Tag Manager and Google Analytics 4 tags load on every page and collect page URL, page title, and page path automatically.</li>
        <li><strong>Through affiliate link clicks:</strong> When you click on an affiliate-marked link, we record the product name, link URL, link text, page URL, and page title.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. How we use information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To send newsletter communications to subscribers.</li>
        <li>To understand how visitors use our website and improve content quality.</li>
        <li>To attribute affiliate link clicks to specific products.</li>
        <li>To respond to your enquiries.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Third-party services</h2>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Service</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Data shared</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Google Tag Manager</td>
            <td>Tag management for analytics and tracking</td>
            <td>Page URL, page title, page path, affiliate link click data</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Google Analytics 4</td>
            <td>Website analytics and reporting</td>
            <td>Page URL, page title, page path, affiliate link click data (via GTM)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Brevo</td>
            <td>Newsletter subscription management</td>
            <td>Email address submitted through the newsletter signup form</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Cloudflare</td>
            <td>Website hosting and infrastructure</td>
            <td>IP addresses and request metadata at the infrastructure level</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>6. Cookies and tracking technologies</h2>
      <p>
        Prismbyte’s application code does not directly set first-party cookies. However, Google Tag Manager and Google Analytics 4 may set their own cookies (such as cookies starting with <code>_ga</code>) when they load on our pages. You can manage or delete cookies through your browser settings.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Data sharing and processing</h2>
      <p>
        Email addresses submitted through the newsletter form are transmitted to Brevo over HTTPS for subscription management. Page usage data and affiliate click data are sent to Google Analytics 4 via Google Tag Manager for analytics and reporting. We do not sell or rent your personal information to third parties.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Data security</h2>
      <p>
        Email addresses submitted through the newsletter form are transmitted to Brevo over HTTPS. Page usage data and affiliate click data are transmitted to Google Analytics 4 via Google Tag Manager. We do not store affiliate click data or page usage data on our own servers; this data is processed by third-party services.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Data retention</h2>
      <p>
        We do not specify retention periods for data processed by third-party services. Retention is governed by the respective privacy policies of Google Analytics 4 and Brevo.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Your privacy rights</h2>
      <p>
        You may contact us at <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> with questions about your personal information or to request access to, correction of, or deletion of your personal information. You may contact us if you wish to stop receiving newsletter communications.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Children's privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Our website is not directed to children under the age of 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this privacy policy from time to time. Changes will be posted on this page.
      </p>

      <h2>13. Contact information</h2>
      <p>
        For questions about this privacy policy or your personal information, contact us at <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>